        "ornament",
        {"colophon": "iti śrī mahābhārate śatasāhasryāṃ saṃhitāyāṃ vaiyāsikyāṃ bhīṣmaparvaṇi śrīmadbhagavadgītā – sūpaniṣatsu brahmavidyāyāṃ yogaśāstre śrī kṛṣṇārjunasaṃvāde karmayogo nāma tṛtīyo'dhyāyaḥ.", "gloss": "Thus, in the Bhagavad Gītā — the Upaniṣad, the knowledge of Brahman, the scripture of yoga, the dialogue of Śrī Kṛṣṇa and Arjuna — within the Bhīṣma Parva of the Mahābhārata, the collection of a hundred thousand verses by Vyāsa, ends the third chapter, Karma Yoga."},
        {"colophon": "iti śrīmatparamahaṃsaparivrājakācāryagovindabhagavatpūjyapādaśiṣyaśrīmacchaṅkarabhagavataḥ kṛtau śrīmadbhagavadgītā bhāṣye karmayogo nāma tṛtīyo'dhyāyaḥ.", "gloss": "Thus ends the third chapter, Karma Yoga, of the commentary on the Bhagavad Gītā composed by Śrī Śaṅkara Bhagavat, wandering ascetic of the highest order and disciple of Śrī Govinda Bhagavatpāda."},
